      "unit": "U3",
      "test": "worker/tests/test_reattach.py — a session ends while no core is attached: it is retained with its ring, its data socket and its manifest entry, a later hello reports ended: true and replays it, and release drops it"
    },
    {
      "unit": "U2",
      "test": "core/internal/session/reattach_test.go — an ended: true handshake is replayed into the recording, the spooled end is written after it, and the core sends release, never live"
    }
  ],
  "description": "An end whose output a core may not have received is retained, not dropped (immortality §4.1, §4.3: never splice silently). Here the session ends while the core is away — its target closed the channel, and the worker spooled the end. The returning core finds it still listed in the manifest and runs the handshake: hello_ack says ended: true, the replay writes the output the core had not committed, and then the core writes the spooled end marker and audit event and sends release in live's place. The worker drops the session only on release, or when its connection closes.",
  "corpus": [
    "immortality §6.1",
    "immortality §4.1",
    "immortality §6.3",
    "immortality §6.4",
    "decision 5.30",
    "plan.md §3 C3",
    "session model §11",
    "session model §15"
  ],
